Appendix I: AI-Native Civic Governance

I.1 The Role of AI

AI is integrated into the civic city at three levels:

Level 1 — Operational. AI optimises HVAC, lighting, mobility scheduling, and resource distribution within dignity constraints. It cannot override human minima.

Level 2 — Participatory. AI synthesises community input, identifies areas of consensus and disagreement, and facilitates deliberation. It does not make decisions.

Level 3 — Strategic. AI models long-term scenarios and their implications for dignity, exergy, and feasibility. It informs human decision-making.

I.2 Constraints on AI

AI systems in the civic city are subject to:

· Dignity constraint: No AI action may violate a dignity threshold.
· Transparency constraint: All AI decisions affecting public resources are explainable.
· Participation constraint: Affected communities must be able to contest AI decisions.
· Privacy constraint: No AI system may collect data beyond what is necessary for its function.
· Human override: Any AI decision may be overridden by human authority.

