Appendix O: Concluding Remarks

This appendix has provided the technical, empirical, institutional, and architectural details that support the main theoretical framework. The mathematical foundations are rigorous; the empirical protocols are operational; the institutional designs are grounded in social choice theory; and the architectural prototypes demonstrate feasibility.

The programme proceeds from mathematics to architecture to institutions to scale. The fundamental questions remain:

\boxed{\text{For which populations, normative thresholds, and physical constraints does the set of dignified cities exist?}}

\boxed{\text{Which part of this set remains thermodynamically admissible?}}

\boxed{\text{What compromise geometry appears in the objective space?}}

Only after these questions are resolved do architecture, institutions, and artificial intelligence enter the analysis. This is the discipline that the framework imposes: feasibility is prior to preference; mathematics is prior to design; dignity is prior to optimisation.

The next phase concerns the quadratic case n = 3, the convexity properties of the objective image, and the empirical calibration of exergy destruction. These are the critical path items. The rest—architecture, institutions, AI—will follow once the mathematical foundation is secure.

